#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Builds spk/ui/i18n.js, the dictionary of the settings screen inside DSM.

The screen is where the package is set up — there is no install wizard — so
it carries the explanations the wizard used to: whoever fills it in has
usually never seen the project and is being asked for a password and a token.
"DSM user" alone does not say which user, and the list of allowed ids does not
explain itself at all.

The page is plain and served by DSM's web server, with no build step and no
bundler, so its translations are generated here and committed; CI regenerates
them and fails on a difference. English is the source of truth; a missing
string falls back to it rather than showing a key. {name} placeholders are
filled in by the page and have to survive every translation.

    tools/make-dsmui-i18n.py
"""
import json
import pathlib
import re

# Order matters only for reading the file: en first, then the rest as in
# web/src/i18n.
